  "name": "ready_stance",
  "note": "(anim-rework S3 keys, real-world standard, keyed by hand; never traced) The drawn-weapon ready stance, standing: feet staggered about 26 cm with the left forward and about hip width apart (add 0), knees soft (22-24 deg), the hips a little lower than the holstered idle, the weight a little forward (the pelvis about 2 cm ahead of the feet centre), the pelvis turned 6 deg right with the stagger and the chest square to the gun (yaw 0), pelvis 6 / chest 4 deg forward, the head upright. Alive over the cycle: two slow breaths, a 0.6 cm sway. Not mirrored. Legs, pelvis and trunk only: the arms are keyed neutral (hanging, elbows 10) because the weapon arms stay procedural (hand IK on the gun). Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up). Pelvis offsets in cm from the standing rest. Arms: flex (+ forward, in the chest frame), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward. Legs (the Blender preview and the track only: the game's feet come from the foot planner): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in toward the midline), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up).",
